# Paths the pre-publish scanner (git-hooks/scan.sh) skips.
# One path per line, exactly as git lists it. Lines starting with # are comments.
# Every entry says why it is here.

# The bundled fonts are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, which requires the
# fonts' own copyright notices to ship with them. The scanner flags any copyright
# notice that is not the repository owner's; these two are the notices OFL asks for.
ui/public/fonts/OFL.txt
ui/public/fonts/README.md

# False positive, temporary: on CI the runner's account name is the same word as
# the last part of the vitest runner package's name, and the scanner's "this
# machine's user name" rule then matches that package's path in the lock file.
# Secrets are covered separately: gitleaks scans the whole history. Remove this
# entry once the shared scanner is fixed on its side.
package-lock.json
